    <worksheet name='1. Income vs Campaigns'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Income vs campaigns</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Average of Income.  Color shows details about Response Total.  The marks are labeled by Response Total.  Details are shown for Response Total.

This boxplot shows whether or not there is an impact of income towards campaign response.

 Based on the boxplot, we can see that there indeed is a correlation. What we see is that Customers who make an average of $48k - which would be the lower outlier- did not respond to campaigns.

And the income where customers started to respond(1) sat higher at about $56k.

- The Box: The middle of the boxplot where 50% of the customers earn, sits higher than the DID NOT RESPOND, showing that higher income customers respond more.
- The Median Line: Median is $70k. The median is higher than the minimum and higher than the lower end of the boxplot that was $56k.
-Dots: The dots were more spread on the Responded side. And can show the outliers where customers that responded more (5 count) made an avg income of about $86k

</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Capstone-Retail Analytics by Inigo Arboleda' name='federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb'>
            <column datatype='integer' name='[Income]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column caption='Response Total' datatype='integer' name='[Response_Total]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Income]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:Income:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Response_Total]' derivation='None' name='[none:Response_Total:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='cell'>
            <format attr='text-format' field='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Income:qk]' value='c&quot;$&quot;#,##0;-&quot;$&quot;#,##0' />
          </style-rule>
        </style>
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Circle' />
            <encodings>
              <color column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[none:Response_Total:ok]' />
              <text column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[none:Response_Total:ok]' />
              <text column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Income:qk]' />
              <lod column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[none:Response_Total:ok]' />
            </encodings>
            <reference-line axis-column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Income:qk]' boxplot-mark-exclusion='false' boxplot-whisker-type='standard' enable-instant-analytics='true' formula='average' id='refline0' label-type='automatic' probability='95' scope='per-cell' symmetric='false' value-column='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Income:qk]' z-order='1' />
            <style>
