    <worksheet name='1. Response Rate by Income Band'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Average Response Rate by Income Band</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run><![CDATA[Average of Response Total for each Income Band.  Color shows details about Income Band.  The marks are labeled by average of Response Total.

Created a calculated field called Income Band to be able to fit the ranges of income into one field.
-Executed through ElseIf statements. 
IF [Income] < 20000 THEN 'Under $20K'
ELSEIF [Income] < 40000 THEN '$20K - $40K'
ELSEIF [Income] < 60000 THEN '$40K - $60K'
ELSEIF [Income] < 80000 THEN '$60K - $80K'
ELSEIF [Income] < 100000 THEN '$80K - $100K'
ELSE 'Over $100K'
END

- What we can see from the chart supports the hypothesis that higher income results into more campaign engagement and lower income leads to fewer campaign engagement]]></run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Capstone-Retail Analytics by Inigo Arboleda' name='federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb'>
            <column caption='Income Band' datatype='string' name='[Calculation_3669419706220555]' role='dimension' type='nominal'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='IF [Income] &lt; 20000 THEN &apos;Under $20K&apos;&#10;ELSEIF [Income] &lt; 40000 THEN &apos;$20K - $40K&apos;&#10;ELSEIF [Income] &lt; 60000 THEN &apos;$40K - $60K&apos;&#10;ELSEIF [Income] &lt; 80000 THEN &apos;$60K - $80K&apos;&#10;ELSEIF [Income] &lt; 100000 THEN &apos;$80K - $100K&apos;&#10;ELSE &apos;Over $100K&apos;&#10;END' />
            </column>
            <column datatype='integer' name='[ID]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
            <column datatype='integer' name='[Income]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column caption='Response Total' datatype='integer' name='[Response_Total]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Response_Total]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:Response_Total:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Response_Total]' derivation='Count' name='[cnt:Response_Total:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[ID]' derivation='CountD' name='[ctd:ID:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Calculation_3669419706220555]' derivation='None' name='[none:Calculation_3669419706220555:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Response_Total]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Response_Total:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <shelf-sorts>
            <shelf-sort-v2 dimension-to-sort='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[none:Calculation_3669419706220555:nk]' direction='ASC' is-on-innermost-dimension='true' measure-to-sort-by='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Response_Total:qk]' shelf='columns' />
          </shelf-sorts>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='axis'>
            <format attr='display' class='0' field='[federated.1axk95m0px4xhh19h5lsh0q82ydb].[avg:Response_Total:qk]' scope='rows' value='false' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='cell'>
