          <formatted-text>
            <run>Total Spend Distribution by Household Type</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Sum of Total Spend.  Color shows details about Household Type.  The marks are labeled by sum of Total Spend and Household Type.

The box plot shows me the distribution of total spend by household type.
- No dependants $703,262 TOTAL
- Teenagers Only $458,835 TOTAL
- Children Only $96,614 TOTAL
- Both children and teenagers $95,044 TOTAL

Shows that customers with No dependants have the highest median spend. And customers with both children and teenagers show the lowest overall spending-supporting the hypothesis that household environement negatively impacts campaign engagement and spending behavior</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
